Project-CarpeDiem
=================

Getting started
---------------

To get started with CarpeDiem, you'll need to get familiar with [Source Control Tools](https://source.android.com/setup/develop).

To initialize your local repository using the CarpeDiem trees, use a command like this:
```
repo init -u https://github.com/Project-CarpeDiem/android.git -b lineage-24.0 --git-lfs
```
Then to sync up:
```
repo sync
```
CarpeDiem is based on LineageOS `lineage-24.0`. See `snippets/carpediem.xml`
for the repositories CarpeDiem forks; everything else tracks upstream.

Build Flags
-----------
```
# Maintainer Name
CARPEDIEM_MAINTAINER := "YourInput" (Default: Unknown)

# Whether Including GMS Prebuilts
WITH_GMS := true/false (Default: true)

# GMS Flavor
GMS_MAKEFILE := gms_mini.mk/gms_full/gms_pico (Default: gms_mini.mk)
```

Setup Environment:
------------------
Navigate to the root directory of Project-CarpeDiem:
```
cd path/to/source
```
Run the environment setup script:
```
. build/envsetup.sh
```
Build Configuration:
--------------------
Choose your device configuration:
```
lunch lineage_$device-$buildtype
```
Replace $device with your device codename and $buildtype with your prefered build type (user, userdebug or eng).
Compilation:
------------
Start the compilation process:
```
m bacon -j$(nproc --all)
```

Submitting patches
------------------
Patches are always welcome! Please submit them via GitHub pull requests
against the `lineage-24.0` branch of the relevant `Project-CarpeDiem` repository.
